  "summary": "Thewa is a special art of jewelry making which involves fusing of intricately worked-out sheet gold on molten glass.",
  "description": "Thewa is a special art of jewelry making which involves fusing of intricately worked-out sheet gold on molten glass. It evolved in Pratapgarh district, Rajasthan India. Its origin dates back to the rajput era.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Rajasthan; registration 2013–14), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
